{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>One who loves</b> — stands in place of two: <b>pure of heart</b>, that is, pure from evil things, which are like dross; and <b>one who loves grace of his lips</b>, meaning a man of grace because he has lips of knowledge. It is also possible that חן is an adjective. And whoever loves both, his greatness increases until the king is his friend — like Hushai the Archite, lover of the pure, who was David's friend."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:10.663735918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}